CHECK:ALLOC_SIZEOF_STRUCT: Prefer kzalloc(sizeof(*clk_gpio_gate)...) over kzalloc(sizeof(struct clk_gpio_gate)...)
#86: FILE: drivers/clk/clk-gpio-gate.c:92:
+	clk_gpio_gate = kzalloc(sizeof(struct clk_gpio_gate), GFP_KERNEL);

The allocation style is bad.  In general for family of
allocation functions using sizeof() to get memory size,
constructs like::

  p = alloc(sizeof(struct foo), ...)

should be::

  p = alloc(sizeof(*p), ...)

See: https://www.kernel.org/doc/html/latest/process/coding-style.html#allocating-memory

